IMPORT prelude

-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7, section 339A (Threshold amounts) -- LAYER 1.
-- Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
-- The threshold amounts feed the exceptions in ss 327(2C) and (2D), 328(5) and (6), 329(2C) and (2D).
-- The amounts are the text's figures at the edition date (2026-06-30); the Secretary of State's power to vary them by order (s 339A(7))
-- is machinery, and an amended figure is a different text.
--
-- SHAPE.  The threshold amount is a number in pounds, so "the text states no amount for this case" is NOTHING.
-- An officer's specification is an input (the person supplies the amount an officer has specified, or none).
-- The powers of the officer (subsections (3) to (5)) are encoded as what the text lets an officer do; the individual meets them
-- through the question "what is my threshold amount?" and "may the officer vary it?".

§ `Section 339A: threshold amounts`

-- s 339A(1) says which subsections serve which exceptions; it is a cross-reference table that creates no rule (coverage table: inert, reason 1).

§§ `s 339A(2): the account threshold`

-- src:762 | (2) The threshold amount for acts done by a deposit-taking body , electronic money institution or payment institution in operating an account is £3,000 unless a higher amount is specified under the following provisions of this section (in which event it is that higher amount).
@ref s 339A(2) (src:762)
GIVEN `the amount specified under subsection (3) or (4), in pounds` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 339A(2) the threshold amount for acts done in operating an account, in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount specified under subsection (3) or (4), in pounds`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 3_000 -- the default amount of subsection (2)
    WHEN JUST higher THEN IF higher GREATER THAN 3_000 THEN higher ELSE 3_000 -- "unless a higher amount is specified": an amount that is not higher leaves the default

§§ `s 339A(3) to (6): who may specify, and the floor`

-- src:763 | (3) An officer of Revenue and Customs, or a constable, may specify the threshold amount for acts done by a deposit-taking body , electronic money institution or payment institution in operating an account—
-- src:764 | (a) when he gives consent, or gives notice refusing consent, to the body's or institution's doing of an act mentioned in section 327(1), 328(1) or 329(1) in opening, or operating, the account or a related account, or
-- src:765 | (b) on a request from the body or institution.
@ref s 339A(3) (src:763-765)
-- s 340(13): "References to a constable include references to a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency".
DECLARE `Who is acting under section 339A` IS ONE OF
    `an officer of Revenue and Customs`
    `a constable`
    `a person authorised for the purposes of this Part by the Director General of the National Crime Agency`
    `another person`

DECLARE `Occasion for specifying a threshold amount` IS ONE OF
    `when giving consent to the doing of an act in opening or operating the account or a related account`
    `when giving notice refusing consent to the doing of an act in opening or operating the account or a related account`
    `on a request from the body or institution`
    `on another occasion`

GIVEN who IS A `Who is acting under section 339A`
      occasion IS A `Occasion for specifying a threshold amount`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339A(3) the person may specify the threshold amount for acts done in operating an account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF who EQUALS `another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An officer of Revenue and Customs, or a constable, may specify"; the subsection is silent about anyone else
        IF occasion EQUALS `on another occasion` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when he gives consent, or gives notice refusing consent" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c): 'when' counts as 'where', so an occasion the subsection does not name is the text's no; a person it does not name stays NOTHING (a power given to named persons, no 'only'))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:766 | (4) Where the threshold amount for acts done in operating an account is specified under subsection (3) or this subsection, an officer of Revenue and Customs, or a constable, may vary the amount (whether on a request from the deposit-taking body , electronic money institution or payment institution or otherwise) by specifying a different amount.
@ref s 339A(4) (src:766)
GIVEN who IS A `Who is acting under section 339A`
      `the threshold amount was specified under subsection (3) or this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339A(4) the person may vary the threshold amount for acts done in operating an account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF who EQUALS `another person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an officer of Revenue and Customs, or a constable, may vary"; silent about anyone else
        IF NOT `the threshold amount was specified under subsection (3) or this subsection` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the threshold amount for acts done in operating an account is specified under subsection (3) or this subsection, an officer of Revenue and Customs, or a constable, may vary the amount" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:767 | (5) Different threshold amounts may be specified under subsections (3) and (4) for different acts done in operating the same account.
@ref s 339A(5) (src:767)
GIVEN `the amounts are specified for different acts done in operating the same account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339A(5) different threshold amounts may be specified for different acts on the same account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amounts are specified for different acts done in operating the same account` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Different threshold amounts may be specified under subsections (3) and (4) for different acts done in operating the same account" says nothing about other cases

-- s 339A(6): a specified amount must, when specified, not be less than the amount in subsection (2).
-- A flat "must not be less than": an amount below £3,000 is not one the text allows an officer to specify.
-- src:768 | (6) The amount specified under subsection (3) or (4) as the threshold amount for acts done in operating an account must, when specified, not be less than the amount specified in subsection (2).
@ref s 339A(6) (src:768)
GIVEN `the amount specified, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339A(6) the specified amount is one that may be specified as the threshold amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount specified, in pounds` AT LEAST 3_000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, when specified, not be less than the amount specified in subsection (2)"

§§ `s 339A(6A) and (8): termination of a relationship, related accounts`

-- src:769 | (6A) The threshold amount for acts done by a person carrying on business in the regulated sector, for the purposes of the termination of a business relationship with a customer or client, is £3,000.
@ref s 339A(6A) (src:769)
GIVEN `the act is done by a person carrying on business in the regulated sector for the purposes of the termination of a business relationship with a customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 339A(6A) the threshold amount for acts done to terminate a business relationship, in pounds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is done by a person carrying on business in the regulated sector for the purposes of the termination of a business relationship with a customer or client` THEN JUST 3_000
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the amount is given "for acts done by a person carrying on business in the regulated sector, for the purposes of the termination of a business relationship"

-- s 339A(7) is a power of the Secretary of State to vary the amounts in (2) and (6A) by order: machinery (coverage table: inert, reason 2).

-- src:771 | (8) For the purposes of this section, an account is related to another if each is maintained with the same deposit-taking body , electronic money institution or payment institution and there is a person who, in relation to each account, is the person or one of the persons entitled to instruct the body or institution as respects the operation of the account.
@ref s 339A(8) (src:771)
GIVEN `each is maintained with the same deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a person who, in relation to each account, is the person or one of the persons entitled to instruct the body or institution as respects the operation of the account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 339A(8) the account is related to the other` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `each is maintained with the same deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution` AND `there is a person who, in relation to each account, is the person or one of the persons entitled to instruct the body or institution as respects the operation of the account`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an account is related to another if" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
